rules.summary:
- {"if": "The patient reports or reflects on panic/anxiety experiences in a vague/subjective way (e.g., 'it was a bad week')", "then": "Prompt the patient to use specific, objective data recorded on standardized forms to clarify and ground the discussion."}
- {"if": "A panic attack occurs", "then": "Instruct the patient to complete the Your Panic Attack Record as soon as possible after the episode."}
- {"if": "It is the end of the day", "then": "Remind the patient to complete the Daily Mood Record, rating average anxiety, depression, and worry about panic for that day."}
- {"if": "Reviewing progress week to week", "then": "Use the Progress Record to visually plot trends in panic attacks and mood ratings and discuss observed patterns with the patient."}
- {"if": "The patient feels increased anxiety about recording", "then": "Validate the feeling, explain the difference between subjective and objective recording, and encourage continued objective documentation using specific forms."}
- {"if": "A panic attack trigger cannot be identified by the patient", "then": "Instruct the patient to record the last thing or situation they noticed before the attack, even if the trigger is unclear."}

- {"if": "Patient describes an episode of anxiety or panic", "then": "Guide the patient to separate and identify physical symptoms, thoughts, and behaviors."}
- {"if": "Patient attributes panic attacks to mysterious or external causes only", "then": "Educate the patient on the cognitive-behavioral cycle, illustrating the interplay between thoughts, symptoms, and behaviors."}
- {"if": "Patient reports ongoing avoidance of certain situations", "then": "Clarify the long-term negative impact of avoidance and link this to the agoraphobia cycle."}
- {"if": "Patient expresses belief that anxiety should be eliminated", "then": "Normalize anxiety as a natural, sometimes helpful emotion, and correct the misconception of total elimination as a goal."}
- {"if": "Beginning a new session or homework check-in", "then": "Review completed self-monitoring forms and discuss observations/insights gained."}
- {"if": "Patient expresses extreme fear about physical symptoms", "then": "Provide psychoeducation about the harmlessness of these symptoms and introduce cognitive restructuring as a future strategy."}
- {"if": "Discussing intervention skills before patient has tracked their symptoms and cycles", "then": "Prioritize self-monitoring and awareness-building before implementing new coping techniques."}
